LOCAL RAG
=========

Local RAG is a Windows-first, self-hosted document search and question-answering
application. It uses Next.js, FastAPI, PostgreSQL with pgvector, RustFS, Ollama,
BAAI bge reranking, and PaddleOCR-VL. Documents, prompts, and answers remain on
the operator's own machine or private LAN deployment.

STATUS

This repository publishes the source tree. The optional signed Personal bundle
is a separate convenience distribution and must not be treated as qualified
until a signed GitHub Release explicitly says so.

QUICK START

Supported developer and Personal source platform: 64-bit Windows 10/11.

Install and start Docker Desktop and Ollama, then install Node.js 20 or newer,
Python 3.12, and uv. Clone this repository and double-click:

    Setup-Local-RAG.cmd

The setup program installs locked source dependencies, prepares isolated local
stores and secrets, downloads the approved Ollama models, builds the web app,
and opens the first-owner setup flow. There is no default username or password.

DEVELOPMENT VALIDATION

    uv --directory apps/api sync --frozen
    pnpm install --frozen-lockfile
    pnpm validate

Hardware-dependent OCR, model, database, object-storage, browser, backup, and
restore checks are intentionally separate from the ordinary source test suite.

PRIVACY AND SECURITY

Never submit real documents, filenames, prompts, answers, credentials, tokens,
environment files, private keys, database dumps, or unrestricted logs. Report
suspected vulnerabilities privately through the repository's GitHub Security
Advisory page; see SECURITY.

